---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const title='Omnichannel retail architecture | Marcelo Ojeda';const description='Architecture story: connecting retail channels, ERP, WMS, inventory and logistics as an evolving omnichannel operation.';
---
<BaseLayout {title} {description} lang="en"><section class="case-intro"><span class="case-no">ARCHITECTURE STORY / 01</span><h1>From B2B to an omnichannel ecosystem.</h1><p class="lede">The challenge was not adding channels. It was making stores, digital commerce, inventory and logistics behave as one operation while the business kept growing.</p></section><div class="case-facts"><div><small>Context</small><strong>Retail · B2B → Omnichannel</strong></div><div><small>Scale</small><strong>50+ stores · ~800K → ~5M units</strong></div><div><small>Focus</small><strong>Integration · operational continuity</strong></div></div><section class="case-body"><div class="prose"><h2>Growth creates coupling.</h2><div><p>Each new channel adds flows, states and dependencies. Treating e-commerce, marketplaces or stores as isolated projects would have fragmented inventory and fulfillment.</p><p>The architectural work was to evolve the integration between commercial channels and the operational core without losing continuity.</p></div></div><div class="system-flow" aria-label="Conceptual system flow"><span class="node">Channels</span><span class="link">→</span><span class="node accent">Integration</span><span class="link">→</span><span class="node">ERP / WMS</span><span class="link">→</span><span class="node">Logistics</span></div><div class="prose"><h2>Decisions over components.</h2><div class="decision-list"><div class="decision"><b>01</b><strong>Integrate the operation</strong><p>Connect commercial channels with core systems instead of duplicating operational truth.</p></div><div class="decision"><b>02</b><strong>Protect continuity</strong><p>Evolve critical order, inventory, warehouse and dispatch flows while operations remain active.</p></div><div class="decision"><b>03</b><strong>Stay implementation-aware</strong><p>Architecture decisions validated through backend, APIs, databases and enterprise integration.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-head"><span class="label">Evolution</span><h2>Fifteen years is not a project. It is a system changing.</h2><p>The architecture had to absorb new channels, more inventory, more physical locations and new integrations without starting over.</p></div><div class="timeline"><div class="timeline-row"><time>BASE</time><strong>B2B operations</strong><p>Enterprise applications and core processes supporting a primarily wholesale operation.</p></div><div class="timeline-row"><time>EXPANSION</time><strong>Physical retail</strong><p>50+ stores introduce new inventory, availability and distributed-operation needs.</p></div><div class="timeline-row"><time>DIGITAL</time><strong>E-commerce + marketplaces</strong><p>New commercial channels must coexist with ERP, inventory, warehousing and fulfillment.</p></div><div class="timeline-row"><time>SCALE</time><strong>~800K → ~5M units</strong><p>The operational platform accompanies substantial growth in managed volume.</p></div><div class="timeline-row"><time>EVOLUTION</time><strong>Java EE → Spring Boot + APIs</strong><p>Incremental modernization without discarding accumulated operational rules.</p></div></div></section><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-head"><span class="label">Ownership</span><h2>More than building features.</h2><p>The role combines historical system knowledge with decisions about how the system should keep changing.</p></div><div class="decision-list"><div class="decision"><b>A</b><strong>Architecture & integration</strong><p>Shape how commercial channels, SAP Business One, WMS, inventory, logistics and external services coexist.</p></div><div class="decision"><b>B</b><strong>Operational continuity</strong><p>Change platforms that support real operations and cannot be treated as prototypes.</p></div><div class="decision"><b>C</b><strong>Modernization</strong><p>Reduce legacy coupling through Spring Boot, REST APIs and more explicit boundaries.</p></div><div class="decision"><b>D</b><strong>Technical reference</strong><p>Connect architecture decisions with implementation, data, integration and business constraints.</p></div></div></section><style>.evidence-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);border-top:1px solid var(--ink);margin-top:2rem}.evidence-grid article{padding:2rem 1.5rem 2rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.evidence-grid article+article{padding-left:1.5rem;border-left:1px solid var(--line)}.evidence-grid b{display:block;font-size:clamp(2.4rem,5vw,5rem);line-height:1;letter-spacing:-.06em;color:var(--accent)}.evidence-grid span{display:block;margin:.7rem 0 1.2rem;font:700 .65rem/1 monospace;text-transform:uppercase}.evidence-grid p,.case-note{color:var(--muted)}.case-note{max-width:760px;font-size:.8rem;margin-top:1rem}@media(max-width:760px){.evidence-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.evidence-grid article+article{padding-left:0;border-left:0}}</style></BaseLayout>